---
title: Salmon piccata
servings: 4
tags: [italian, seafood, weeknight, quick]
cuisine: italian
time: 22 minutes
source: Salmon Piccata by Gina Matsoukas, Running to the Kitchen, https://www.runningtothekitchen.com/salmon-piccata/
---

Pat the @salmon{2}(fillets, about 6 oz each) dry. Mix the
@all-purpose flour{1/4%cup}, @salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{1/4%tsp} in a
shallow dish, coat the fish, and shake off the excess.

Heat the @extra virgin olive oil{1%tbsp} and 1 tbsp of the
@unsalted butter{2%tbsp} in a large #skillet{} over medium-high heat. Sear the
salmon until browned on both sides, then move it to a clean plate.

Turn the heat to medium and melt the rest of the butter in the same pan. Add
the @shallot{1}(large, minced), @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) and
@capers{1/3%cup} and cook ~{1%minute}.

Pour in the @lemon juice{1/3%cup}(about 2 lemons) and @chicken broth{2/3%cup}
and bring to a simmer. Let it reduce ~{5%minutes}, then season.

Put the salmon back, spoon the sauce over and warm it through ~{1%minute}.

Off the heat, finish with @parsley{}(chopped) and @lemon{}(slices).
